IMPORT prelude

-- Fees Act 1920 (Singapore) -- what the Minister for Finance may levy by order and where (s 2), when an order takes effect (s 3),
-- the officer's right to refuse to act until paid (s 4), summary recovery and proof of non-payment (s 5), payment by stamps or in
-- money (ss 6, 7), fees fixed by other written law (s 8), remission (s 9) and the validation of past late-payment collections (s 10).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/FeA1920.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is "[Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]", against ss 2, 3, 5, 8, 9 and 10. The deposit's metadata
-- records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0151 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is ten sections long, so the whole operative text (ss 2 to 10) is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (short title)
-- and every actual fee amount -- those are fixed by orders under s 2, none of which was retrieved -- and the Gazette and
-- presentation-to-Parliament duties of s 3(a), (c) beyond the point that effect runs from publication.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fees Act 1920 -- levies`

DECLARE Levy IS ONE OF
    `a licence fee`
    `a permit fee`
    `another fee or payment`
    `a late-payment charge or penalty`
    `interest on an outstanding amount`
    `interest for payment by instalment`

DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `a subordinate court`
    `a public office or department`
    `a private business`

-- Where the amount of a levy comes from: an order under s 2, or another written law that itself fixes the amount (s 8).
DECLARE Source IS ONE OF
    `an order under section 2`
    `another written law fixing the amount`

DECLARE PaymentMethod IS ONE OF
    `by stamps`
    `in money`
    `as the order or law otherwise provides`

DECLARE Remitter IS ONE OF
    `the Minister for Finance`
    `a person named in the section 2 order`
    `the collecting officer`

§§ `2 -- what may be prescribed, and where`

-- s 2: "The Minister for Finance may by order prescribe -- (a) the fees and payments for licences, permits and otherwise; (b) the
-- charges and penalties for the late payment of any fee or payment referred to in paragraph (a); and (c) the interest payable on any
-- outstanding amount of any fee, payment, charge or penalty referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) or for any payment thereof by
-- instalment, that are leviable or to be leviable, in the subordinate courts of civil and criminal jurisdiction, and in all public
-- offices and departments."
--
-- Every kind of levy in the Levy list falls within (a), (b) or (c); what limits the power is WHERE the levy is charged.
GIVEN `the levy` IS A Levy, `the levying body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may prescribe it by order` IF
    CONSIDER `the levying body`
    WHEN `a subordinate court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a public office or department` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- when an order takes effect`

-- s 3: "Every order under section 2 shall -- (a) be published in the Gazette; (b) have effect from the date of the publication; and
-- (c) be presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication."
--
-- Effect runs from publication. The text does not make effect wait for presentation to Parliament, so presentation is not an input.
-- Dates are yyyymmdd numbers.
GIVEN `published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN, `publication date` IS A NUMBER, `the date in question` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order has effect` IF
    `published in the Gazette` AND `the date in question` AT LEAST `publication date`

§§ `4 -- officer may decline to act until paid`

-- s 4: "The officer of any court, public office or department required to do anything for which a fee or payment is chargeable
-- under this Act may decline to do that thing until the fee is paid or the payment is made."
--
-- The right is to DECLINE, not a duty to refuse: the officer may still act unpaid. It turns on the fee or payment for the thing
-- itself; the text says nothing of an unpaid late charge or interest.
GIVEN `a fee or payment is chargeable for the thing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fee or payment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may decline to do it` IF
    `a fee or payment is chargeable for the thing` AND (NOT `the fee or payment has been made`)

§§ `5 -- summary recovery and proof of non-payment`

-- s 5(1): "All fees, payments, charges, penalties and interest prescribed in any order under section 2 shall be recoverable when not
-- otherwise provided for by summary procedure before a Magistrate's Court in the manner provided for the recovery of fines and
-- penalties before a Magistrate's Court, on complaint by or on behalf of the officer to whom [they] ought to have been paid ..."
-- (2): "A certificate by such officer that the fee, charge, penalty or interest has not been paid, or that the payment has not been
-- made, shall be held to be prima facie proof of non-payment."
--
-- s 5(1) reaches only levies "prescribed in any order under section 2"; a fee whose amount another written law fixes is not
-- brought in by it.
GIVEN `the source` IS A Source, `recovery is otherwise provided for` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer complains` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is recoverable summarily before a Magistrate's Court` IF
        (CONSIDER `the source`
         WHEN `an order under section 2` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (NOT `recovery is otherwise provided for`)
    AND `the officer complains`

-- "prima facie proof" -- INFERENCE: proof that stands unless displaced. Whether contrary evidence displaces it is not in the text;
-- the input below models that common reading and is labelled as such.
GIVEN `the officer certifies non-payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `contrary evidence is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-payment is proved` IF
    `the officer certifies non-payment` AND (NOT `contrary evidence is accepted`)

§§ `6, 7 -- payment by stamps or in money`

-- s 6: the Minister may by order declare that "all or any fees or payments for licences or permits in any of the subordinate courts
-- of civil and criminal jurisdiction, public offices and departments ... shall be payable by means of stamps".
-- s 7: the Minister may by order declare that "all or any fees or payments in any of the public offices and departments now made
-- payable by means of stamps shall be paid in money, notwithstanding any Act in force to the contrary".
--
-- s 7 names public offices and departments only, not the subordinate courts. A s 7 order therefore converts a stamps fee back to
-- money in an office or department, but on the text not in a court. s 6 reaches only licence and permit fees.
GIVEN `the levy` IS A Levy, `the levying body` IS A Body, `a section 6 stamps order covers it` IS A BOOLEAN, `a section 7 money order covers it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PaymentMethod
DECIDE `how it is to be paid` IS
    IF `a section 7 money order covers it` AND `stamps reach it` AND `the levying body` EQUALS `a public office or department`
    THEN `in money`
    ELSE IF `stamps reach it`
         THEN `by stamps`
         ELSE `as the order or law otherwise provides`
    WHERE
        `licence or permit` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the levy`
            WHEN `a licence fee` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a permit fee` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `stamps reach it` MEANS
            `a section 6 stamps order covers it` AND `licence or permit` AND (NOT (`the levying body` EQUALS `a private business`))

§§ `8 -- fees fixed by other written law`

-- s 8: "Nothing in this Act shall be held to affect the amount of any fee, payment, charge, penalty or interest leviable or
-- chargeable under any written law in force when express provision is made as to the amount ... in that written law."
GIVEN `the source` IS A Source
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order under this Act may change the amount` IF
    CONSIDER `the source`
    WHEN `another written law fixing the amount` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `9 -- remission`

-- s 9(1): "Notwithstanding section 8, it shall be lawful for the Minister for Finance to remit wholly or in part, and either generally
-- or in any particular case or class of cases, any fee, payment, charge, penalty or interest prescribed under this Act or under any
-- other written law."
-- (2): in an order under s 2 the Minister "may ... provide for the remission of any such fees ... and may specify in the order the
-- person by whom remissions shall be granted."
--
-- The Minister's power reaches fees fixed by OTHER written law too, despite s 8. A named delegate's power exists only under a s 2
-- order that names them; a collecting officer has none unless named.
GIVEN `the source` IS A Source, `who` IS A Remitter, `the order names that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may remit it` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the Minister for Finance` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `the order names that person` AND `the source` EQUALS `an order under section 2`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the lesser of` IS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- "wholly or in part": a remission cannot take the amount below nil.
GIVEN `amount due` IS A NUMBER, `amount remitted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `amount payable after remission` IS
    `amount due` MINUS `the lesser of` `amount due` `amount remitted`

§§ `10 -- validation of past late-payment collections`

-- s 10: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or purportedly
-- as -- (a) a charge or penalty for the late payment of any fee or payment under this Act; or (b) interest on any outstanding amount
-- of any such fee or payment or for any payment thereof by instalment, shall be deemed to be and always to have been validly
-- collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie ... on account of or in respect of any such collection."
--
-- The deposit does not state the commencement date of the 2008 Act, so the input is whether the collection came before it.
GIVEN `the levy` IS A Levy, `collected before the 2008 Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the collection is deemed valid and proceedings are barred` IF
        `collected before the 2008 Act commenced`
    AND (CONSIDER `the levy`
         WHEN `a late-payment charge or penalty` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `interest on an outstanding amount` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `interest for payment by instalment` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
